\name{cellucid_history_bookmark_set}
\alias{cellucid_history_bookmark_set}
\title{Bookmark a step}
\usage{
cellucid_history_bookmark_set(viewer, step, name)
}
\arguments{
\item{viewer}{A viewer \code{\link{cellucid_view}()} or \code{\link{cellucid_serve}()} returned.}
\item{step}{A step of the tracker in use, by its id (history_get lists the steps). Text. Required.}
\item{name}{The bookmark, or null to remove it. Text or \code{NULL} (at least 1 character). Required.}
}
\value{
A \code{cellucid_action_request}, at once and invisibly: the action is sent now, or when the viewer's channel opens.
\code{\link{cellucid_action_result}(request)} returns its outcome: a list of \code{bookmark}, \code{journal}, \code{step}.
}
\description{
Give a step a bookmark name, unique in its tracker (jump to it by name), or remove it with null. Bookmark before destructive or heavy work.
}
\details{
The viewer's action \code{history.bookmark.set} (History). It moves the viewer's history, as the person's Undo, Redo or a click on a step does: it makes no step of the history.
}
\seealso{
\code{\link{cellucid_act}()} sends any action by its type, and \code{\link{cellucid_action_result}()}
collects its answer.
}
\examples{
if (interactive() && requireNamespace("SeuratObject", quietly = TRUE)) {
  data("pbmc_small", package = "SeuratObject")
  viewer <- cellucid_view(SeuratObject::UpdateSeuratObject(pbmc_small))
  request <- cellucid_history_bookmark_set(viewer, name = "Before reclustering",
      step = "s3")
  print(request)
  # cellucid_action_result(request) waits for its outcome.
  cellucid_stop(viewer)
}
}
